TCLAP - Templatized Command Line Argument Parser

This is a simple C++ library that facilitates parsing command line
arguments in a type independent manner. It doesn't conform exactly
to either the GNU or POSIX standards, although it is close. See
docs/manual.html for descriptions of how things work or look at the
simple examples in the examples dir.

Branches
--------

This repository has several long-lived branches:

  1.2  Stable, backwards-compatible version with only critical bug fixes.
  1.4  Current stable version; no new feature development. Should be used
       by most projects requiring C++98 compatibility. Mostly source
       compatible with 1.6.
  1.6  Same as 1.4, but updated to work with modern (C++20 and later)
       versions of C++. Mostly source compatible with 1.4.
  2.0  Reworked library for modern C++ (C++20). Not stable, may break
       API. New features may appear.

Any and all feedback is welcome at https://sf.net/p/tclap/discussion/
